# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 usual.cc atan and tan. An exact argument on atan's cut (re(z)=0, |im(z)|>1) stayed symbolic, and Giac's exact rules then read it on the other side of the cut from the principal value (mpmath, C99 catan: atan(2*i) = pi/2+0.549i, atan(-2*i) = -pi/2-0.549i): cos(atan(z)) = sqrt(1/(z^2+1)) gave i*sqrt(3)/3 for 2*i and for -2*i (right -i*sqrt(3)/3), so a stored w:=atan(2*i) or f(x):=cos(atan(x)) at 2*i showed the wrong sign; arg(atan(2*i)) added pi (atanasln's real part -pi/2). atan returns the principal value sign(t)*pi/2-atan(1/z), t=im(z), exact, with 1/z inside the cut; tan(b+(k+1/2)*pi) is -1/tan(b) where tan(b) has a closed form, so tan(atan(2*i)) stays 2*i. Off the cut, and for a float argument (atanasln), atan is unchanged.
